	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE:\nSince the ADM1270 is designed to control a P-MOS transistor, the RS1E260 was selected as it has a high current capacity (80A) and good enough voltage tolerance (30V).\n\nCurrent limit foldback protection is implemented using the FLB pin and a two-resistor divider: R_A = 1.0MOhm, R_B = 133kOmega. The ISET pin sets the nominal current limit reference voltage to V_ISET = 1.4V. The foldback divider is designed to match this reference at V_OUT = 12V, ensuring that the current limit starts reducing when VOUT drops below 12V to protect the MOSFET's Safe Operating Area (SOA). Above 12V, the current limit is determined by the VISET pin. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 384.81 82.55 0)
		(size 21.59 74.93)
		(margins 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525 1.3525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "52d9cbda-7b28-4a3c-80d3-cd4dad33c739")
	)
